<entry>
  <id>https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/packaging/packages/chromium/-/commit/e8c74b6fdcb9e6b1a8dbe7575e8179eeba69ff53</id>
  <link href="https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/packaging/packages/chromium/-/commit/e8c74b6fdcb9e6b1a8dbe7575e8179eeba69ff53"/>
  <title>upgpkg: 153.0.8010.36-1: New upstream release</title>
  <updated>2026-09-11T14:47:08+02:00</updated>
  <media:thumbnail width="40" height="40" url="https://gitlab.archlinux.org/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/1466/avatar.png?v=1792657452"/>
  <author>
    <name>Christian Heusel</name>
    <email>gromit@archlinux.org</email>
  </author>
  <summary type="html">
- Rebase chromium-149-drop-unknown-clang-flag.patch and
  chromium-152-fix-gn-no-public_inputs.patch for upstream context drift
  in 153.
- Rename chromium-152-crubit.patch to chromium-153-crubit.patch, adding
  back the third_party/blink font_format revert from
  ungoogled-chromium#3946 on top of the existing cbor Rust-bindings
  gating (dropping the latter broke gn gen: unresolved crubit/cbor
  Rust deps).
- Drop chromium-152-dawn-llvm-22.patch: obsolete, upstream dawn no
  longer emits the flags it reverted.
- Add chromium-153-hermetic-python.patch and chromium-153-typescript.patch,
  both from ungoogled-chromium#3946: use system python3 as the GN
  script_executable, disable the native tsgo TypeScript compiler for
  WebUI, and point devtools' typescript.py at the system tsc.
- Add chromium-153-iamf-tools-unbundled-opus.patch: third_party/iamf_tools
  includes vendored Opus via relative "include/opus.h" paths that only
  resolve against a real bundled Opus checkout; use the full
  third_party/opus/src/include/... path instead, matching other unbundled
  Opus consumers.
- Add 'typescript' to makedepends.
- Update REUSE.toml for the patch churn above.

